<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Fitzwilton H1 pretax profit up 13 pct.</title>
<headline>Fitzwilton H1 pretax profit up 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>					  (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		1.37		   vs 1.45</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.1		    vs 1.05</p>
<p> Pretax		     5.11		   vs 4.55</p>
<p> Turnover		   147.41		 vs 147.31</p>
<p> Operating profit	 8.49		   vs 8.12</p>
<p> Interest charge	  5.20		   vs 4.40</p>
<p> Tax charge		 1.14		   vs 1.13</p>
<p> Net taxed		  3.96		   vs 4.22</p>
<p> Attributable	     3.54		   vs 3.69</p>
<p> Record date   10 December 1996</p>
<p> Pay date	31 January 1997</p>
<p>Ex-dividend date 2 December 1996</p>
<p>NOTE - Industrial holding group Fitzwilton Plc, whose principle business is Wellworth, Northern Ireland's leading food retailer, said progress in the first half has continued and leads the company to be confident on the outcome for the year.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom 353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
